# Normalise line endings so a clone on any OS produces working files.
#
# The .cmd launchers in admin/ are the reason this file exists. Batch files must
# have CRLF endings — a .cmd checked out with LF fails in ways that look nothing
# like a line-ending problem (a `for /f` loop silently reads nothing, a label
# jump lands in the wrong place). Forcing eol=crlf means they survive a clone on
# Linux or macOS and still work when copied back to Windows.
* text=auto
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touch, never diff.
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.exe binary

# Generated. Marking them keeps `git diff` and PR reviews readable: nobody needs
# to scroll 200 icon path strings to find the one line that changed by hand.
assets/icons.js linguist-generated=true
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true
